language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Guess the ages of three sons from the product, the sum, and the oldest son's eye colour.
find A1, A2, A3 : int(1..36)

branching on [A1, A2, A3]

such that
$ the product of their ages is 36
A1 * A2 * A3 = 36,
$ A1 is the oldest and A2, A3 are their ages from oldest to youngest
A1 >= A2,
A2 >= A3,
A3 >= 1,
$ the oldest son has blue eyes, so the oldest son is uniquely identified
A1 > A2,
$ the sum of their ages is the number of windows, and the mathematician still needs more information,
$ so another triple of ages with product 36 has the same sum
(exists b1, b2, b3 : int(1..36) .
    (b1 >= b2 /\ b2 >= b3 /\ b1 * b2 * b3 = 36 /\ b1 + b2 + b3 = A1 + A2 + A3 /\
     (b1 != A1 \/ b2 != A2 \/ b3 != A3))),
$ the mathematician now knows the ages, so among the triples with product 36 and the same sum
$ whose oldest son is uniquely identified, there is only one: the answer
forAll b1, b2, b3 : int(1..36) .
    ((b1 >= b2 /\ b2 >= b3 /\ b1 * b2 * b3 = 36 /\ b1 + b2 + b3 = A1 + A2 + A3 /\ b1 > b2 /\ b1 > b3)
     -> (b1 = A1 /\ b2 = A2 /\ b3 = A3))
